    <div class="jr-answer">
      <h2>The short answer</h2>
      <p><strong>No. Collagen is an animal protein, so every collagen supplement on the Indian market comes from fish, cows, pigs or chicken, including our own.</strong> Products sold as plant-based or vegan collagen usually contain no collagen at all; they are blends of vitamin C, zinc, copper and amino acids that support the body's own collagen production.</p>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>Our own products:</strong> Collabloom and Skelecoll are made from hydrolysed marine collagen, from fish. They are non-vegetarian and not suitable for vegetarians, Jains or anyone with a fish allergy.</li>
        <li><strong>The label to check:</strong> under FSSAI rules, anything containing fish or other marine animals must carry the brown non-veg symbol on the front of the pack, whatever the percentage.</li>
        <li><strong>Lab-made collagen:</strong> fermentation-derived, animal-free collagen-like proteins exist, but published human evidence for them is still missing.</li>
        <li><strong>What vegetarians can do:</strong> enough total protein, vitamin C, daily sunscreen and not smoking protect your own collagen better than any boost blend.</li>
      </ul>
    </div>

